There is a problem here.  Now I may have it all wrong, being a purveyor of 
free liberties and such, but if I find a system file that is world readable
I just may read it.  Why?  Because I want to learn.  I have learned more about
unix by reading endless script files and source code than through any book.
What do I do with this knowledge?  Simply satisfy my curiosity.  I have NEVER
seen a world readable system file that contained information that could be 
